### 3. Models / Schemas (Pydantic v2)

#### [NEW] [models/lead.py](file:///d:/Programming/lead-desk/backend/app/models/lead.py)

| Field | Type | Validation |
|-------|------|-----------|
| `name` | `str` | Required, 2–100 chars |
| `email` | `EmailStr` | Required, valid email |
| `budget_range` | `str` | Required, must be one of: `"Under $1,000"`, `"$1,000 – $5,000"`, `"$5,000 – $10,000"`, `"$10,000 – $25,000"`, `"$25,000+"` |
| `message` | `str` | Required, 10–2000 chars |
| `status` | `str` | Default `"New"`, one of: `New`, `Contacted`, `Closed` |
| `created_at` | `datetime` | Auto-set on creation |
| `updated_at` | `datetime` | Auto-set on creation + updated on mutation |

Request schema (`LeadCreate`), response schema (`LeadResponse`), update schema (`LeadStatusUpdate`), and DB schema (`LeadInDB`) will be separate Pydantic models.

#### [NEW] [models/user.py](file:///d:/Programming/lead-desk/backend/app/models/user.py)
- `AdminUserInDB`: `username`, `hashed_password`, `created_at`
- `LoginRequest`: `username`, `password`
- `TokenResponse`: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `token_type`

