### 4. Auth System

#### [NEW] [services/auth_service.py](file:///d:/Programming/lead-desk/backend/app/services/auth_service.py)
- Password hashing with `passlib` + `bcrypt`
- JWT creation (access + refresh) signed with `JWT_SECRET_KEY` via `python-jose`
- Each token includes a unique `jti` (JWT ID) claim for blacklisting
- Token verification: checks expiry, validates signature, checks blacklist
- Blacklist storage: `token_blacklist` collection in MongoDB with TTL index so expired entries auto-delete

#### [NEW] [routers/auth.py](file:///d:/Programming/lead-desk/backend/app/routers/auth.py)

| Endpoint | Method | Auth | Description |
|----------|--------|------|-------------|
| `/auth/login` | POST | Public | Verify credentials → return access + refresh tokens |
| `/auth/refresh` | POST | Bearer (refresh) | Issue new access token, rotate refresh token |
| `/auth/logout` | POST | Bearer | Blacklist current token's `jti` |
| `/auth/me` | GET | Bearer | Return current admin user info |

#### [NEW] [dependencies.py](file:///d:/Programming/lead-desk/backend/app/dependencies.py)
- `get_current_admin`: FastAPI `Depends` that extracts + validates the JWT from `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, checks blacklist, looks up user in DB → returns user or raises `401`

#### [NEW] [scripts/seed_admin.py](file:///d:/Programming/lead-desk/backend/scripts/seed_admin.py)
- CLI script run via `python -m scripts.seed_admin`
- Prompts for username and password interactively (uses `getpass` for password)
- Hashes password with bcrypt, inserts into `users` collection
- Refuses to create if a user with the same username already exists
- No credentials hardcoded anywhere

